    "text": "To determine how many goldfish the pet store owner sold in one week, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the profit per goldfish:**\n   - Cost to buy a goldfish: $0.25\n   - Selling price of a goldfish: $0.75\n   - Profit per goldfish: \\(0.75 - 0.25 = 0.50\\) dollars\n\n2. **Determine the total amount of money the owner has after one week:**\n   - The tank costs $100.\n   - The owner is 45% short of the price, so he has 55% of the price.\n   - Amount of money the owner has: \\(100 \\times 0.55 = 55\\) dollars\n\n3. **Calculate the number of goldfish sold:**\n   - Profit per goldfish: $0.50\n   - Total amount of money: $55\n   - Number of goldfish sold: \\(\\frac{55}{0.50} = 110\\)\n\nThus, the number of goldfish sold in one week is \\(\\boxed{110}\\).",
